DTSTART:20260629T233000Z
DTEND:20260630T013000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall &amp\; LIVE@jacobs
SUMMARY:Winston Choi\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Repertoire  Ravel: Jeux d'eau (1901)Mischa Zupko: Etude No. 2.
  Rain (2001)Takemitsu: Rain Tree Sketch No. 2 (1992)Ligeti: Étude No. 5.
  Arc-en-ciel (1985)Debussy: 'Reflets dans l'eau' from "Images I" (1905)Tr
 istan Murail: Cailloux dans l'eau (2017)Szymanowski: 'L'île des Sirènes
 ' from "Métopes\, Op. 29" (1915)Ravel: 'Ondine' from "Gaspard de la nuit
 " (1908)Beach: By the Still Waters\, Op. 114 (1925)Bonis: Barcarolle\, Op
 . 71 (1905)Decaux: Clair de lune No. 4. La mer (1903)Dupont: 'Houles' fro
 m "La maison dans les dunes" (1909)Lei Liang: 'Seven Rays of the Sun' fro
 m "My Windows" (2007)Berio: 'Wasserklavier' from "Six Encores" (1990)Bria
 n Current: Far Beyond Things Finite – Epilogue: The River of Light (201
 8)Godowsky: 'The Ruined Water Castle at Djokja' from "Java Suite" (1925)A
 bout the Artist  Canadian pianist Winston Choi is professor and program d
 irector of piano at Roosevelt University's Chicago College of Performing 
 Arts. Winner of France's Concours International de Piano 20e siècle d'Or
 léans and laureate of the Honens International Piano Competition\, he is
  internationally recognized for his bold interpretations of the standard 
 repertoire and his unwavering commitment to contemporary music. He appear
 s worldwide as a soloist\, chamber musician\, and educator. Choi has perf
 ormed concertos with numerous North American and international orchestras
 \, including the Civic Orchestra of Chicago\, Calgary Philharmonic\, Vict
 oria Symphony\, l'Orchestre National de Lille\, and Colombia's national o
 rchestra. His solo recitals have brought him to such major venues as Carn
 egie-Weill Recital Hall\, the Kennedy Center\, and France's Salle Cortot.
  A prolific chamber musician\, he tours widely as a member of Civitas Ens
 emble\, Duo Diorama (with violinist MingHuan Xu)\, and Trio Diorama (with
  Xu and cellist Nick Photinos)\, and recently performed with Matthias Goe
 rne at the Ravinia Festival. A passionate advocate for new music\, Choi h
 as premiered and commissioned over 100 works. His recordings include Elli
 ott Carter's complete piano music\, Jacques Lenot's works (winner of the 
 Grand Prix du Disque)\, and music by Thomas Adès. He appears on such lab
 els as BIS\, Cedille\, and Naxos\, and is a core member of Ensemble Dal N
 iente. He earned degrees from Indiana and Northwestern Universities\, and
  studied with Menahem Pressler and Ursula Oppens. A dedicated pedagogue\,
  Choi is also in demand as a master class clinician and conference presen
 ter\, sharing insights on phrasing\, technique\, and interpretation.
